  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through Friday)\nIssued at 1226 AM CDT SAT AUG 29 2026\n\nWeak upper level low continues to meander across the Gulf coast this \nevening, and will continue to do so through at least Saturday. That \nwill keep the focus of diurnal convection to our south. Latest \ncomputer model runs are in a bit more agreement in handling that \nshortwave energy, largely shearing it out and scooting it westward \nacross the northern Gulf.\n\nAs we get into Sunday, and then especially early next week, the big \nupper level high shifts from the western states to the east. This \nwill put a cap on most convection in our area, and allow \ntemperatures to climb well back up into the 90s. Another round of \nHeat Advisories is becoming more likely starting around Tuesday or \nWednesday of next week.\n\n/61/",
